Title: FOG LINE
Author: James O'Brien
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. FRONT LINE TRENCH - DAWN

Fog erases no-man's-land. SERGEANT TOM HALE, 28, checks his squad — RIVERS, KOWALSKI, NGUYEN. Artillery rumbles distant, rhythmic.
HALE
Stand-to. Eyes on the wire.

INT. DUGOUT - DAY

Hale reads orders by lantern. A map shows a German listening post 200 meters out — marked for capture, not kill.
HALE
We bring back papers, not souvenirs. Quiet in, quiet out.

EXT. NO-MAN'S-LAND - NIGHT

The squad crawls through mud and wire. Flares burst — Kowalski freezes. Hale, thirty-one and steady, pulls him down inches from a trip line.
HALE
(whisper)
Breathe. Move on my count.

INT. ENEMY LISTENING POST - NIGHT

Close quarters. Nguyen covers the door. Hale shoves a satchel against the lone operator — young, barely shaving.
HALE
Papers. Radio codes. Nobody dies if you choose fast.

EXT. ALLIED TRENCH - PREDAWN

The squad drops back over the parapet, satchel secure. Hale stares at the captured map — coordinates match their own sector.
HALE
Three hundred meters of mud for this. They weren't listening to us. They were marking us for tomorrow.

FADE OUT.


THE END
